<mujoco model="open_duck_mini_v2_scaled_wheeled">

  <!--
    Super Duck: wheeled Open Duck Mini v2 (BDX droid style), GIM6010-8 hip-pitch / knee variant.
    Body tree and names follow apirrone/Open_Duck_Mini (`open_duck_mini_v2.xml`):
      `base` -> `trunk_assembly` ->
        * Left leg:  `hip_roll_assembly` (fixed hip mount) -> `left_roll_to_pitch_assembly` -> `knee_and_ankle_assembly`
                     -> `knee_and_ankle_assembly_2` -> `foot_assembly` (driven wheel)
        * Right leg: `hip_roll_assembly_2` -> `right_roll_to_pitch_assembly` -> `knee_and_ankle_assembly_3`
                     -> `knee_and_ankle_assembly_4` -> `foot_assembly_2` (driven wheel)
        * Neck/Head: `neck_pitch_assembly` -> `head_pitch_to_yaw` -> `neck_yaw_assembly` -> `head_assembly`
                     -> `left/right_antenna` (the Open Duck Mini v2 neck and head at 1:1, same STS3215 servos)
    Actuators: 4x SteadyWin GIM6010-8 (hip pitch, knee), 4x GIM4305-10 (hip roll, wheel hubs), 4x STS3215 (neck),
    2x 9 g micro servos (antennas). Sensors: ICM-42688-P IMU (`imu` site), wheel encoders and touch, stereo Camera
    Module 3 eyes (`left/right_eye_cam`, 80 mm baseline), USB nav camera (`trunk_nav_cam`).

    Geometry and mass are the FreeCAD assembly (cad/freecad/super_duck.FCStd): cad/freecad/export_sim.py writes every
    body's meshes (assets/cad/), inertial, collision hulls, the neck body positions, cameras, projector light and
    IMU site. Joint positions, axes and ranges of the legs, actuators, sensors and the keyframe are hand-written here
    (the CAD is built from them through tools/export_cad_spec.py -> cad/hardpoints.json). Re-export after a CAD change.
  -->

